{"key": "39dd587424d07c6fba2faa305aa7cc375c1a418b7212029ce8f1621c83481dba", "value": {"response": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Write a function that takes an integer a and returns True \n    if this ingeger is a cube of some integer number.\n    Note: you may assume the input is always valid.\n    Examples:\n    iscube(1) ==> True\n    iscube(2) ==> False\n    iscube(-1) ==> True\n    iscube(64) ==> True\n    iscube(0) ==> True\n    iscube(180) ==> False\n    '''\n    if a < 0:\n        a = -a\n    return round(a ** (1. / 3)) ** 3 == a\n```", "prompt_eval_count": 828, "eval_count": 143}}
